{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Let them fear it</b> — you will find the word נשף for the beginning of the night and for its end." "<b>on the eyelids of dawn</b> — Some say: like השקפה, and similar to it: התעיף עיניך בו ואיננו (Job 20:9). But the correct interpretation is that it is by way of metaphor with eyes, and dawn is likened to them. The matter is: when dawn opens its eyelids like eyes that have eyelids — and that is the pupil, and it is called עפעף on account of the hole."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:37.185124916Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}